  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BLACK GIRLS SURF</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ngor Surg Camp in Dakar, Senegal, implemented by Black Girls Surf aims to contribute to the social empowerment of girls aged 7-17 but using sports as an entry point to social, economic, health, and environmental awareness. The project will include a number of activities including sporting activities, education, community work, leadership and cultural empowerment, health and wellness workshops, and environmental education. The project aims to provide 60 girls with access to a safe, empowering surf and education camp, increase their knowledge of ocean safety, marine ecosystems, and climate change, develop confidence, leadership, and physical health in the participating youth and foster cultural exchange and build community resilience.</narrative>
  </description>
